#. Activity log summary for an older entry that only recorded that the permission overrides of a voice channel were changed, without saying which. A permission override is a channel-level exception to the permissions of a role or member. It allows or denies chosen permissions in one channel or category only. Use the same word for override as the channel permissions settings, such as Add override. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the channel, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts:138
msgid "{actor} changed the permission overrides of the voice channel {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} đã thay đổi các quyền ghi đè của kênh thoại {channel}"

#. Activity log summary when a member replaced the vanity URL, the custom invite link of the community. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {oldCode} is the previous vanity URL code and {newCode} is the new vanity URL code, both shown as boxed text.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogGuildMessages.ts:25
msgid "{actor} changed the vanity URL from {oldCode} to {newCode}"
msgstr "{actor} đã đổi URL tùy chỉnh từ {oldCode} thành {newCode}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who replaced the avatar on their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The avatar belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts:155
msgid "{actor} changed their community profile avatar"
msgstr "{actor} đã thay đổi ảnh đại diện hồ sơ cộng đồng của họ"

#. Activity log summary for a member who replaced the banner image on their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The banner belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts:170
msgid "{actor} changed their community profile banner"
msgstr "{actor} đã thay đổi ảnh bìa hồ sơ cộng đồng của họ"

#. Activity log summary for a member who changed the bio on their community profile. A community profile is the profile a member uses only in this community, in place of their global profile. The bio belongs to the member, not to the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {text} is the new bio, shown as boxed text and shortened when long.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts:185
msgid "{actor} changed their community profile bio to {text}"
msgstr "{actor} đã thay đổi tiểu sử hồ sơ cộng đồng của họ thành {text}"

#. Activity log summary for a member who changed their own nickname in the community. "Their" means the same member as {actor}. {actor} is that member, shown as a clickable user chip. {oldNick} is the previous nickname and {newNick} is the new nickname. Keep {oldNick} as the old value and {newNick} as the new value. The app shows both in bold, so do not add ** or <b>.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogMemberMessages.ts:80
msgid "{actor} changed their nickname from {oldNick} to {newNick}"
msgstr "{actor} đã đổi biệt danh của mình từ {oldNick} thành {newNick}"

#. Activity log summary for a new webhook when its name was not recorded. {actor} is the member who created the webhook, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogInviteWebhookMessages.ts:95
msgid "{actor} created a webhook"
msgstr "{actor} đã tạo một webhook"

#. Activity log summary when a channel category was created. {actor} is the member who made the change, shown as a clickable user chip, or the word System. {channel} is the new category, shown as a channel chip with its name.
#: src/features/guild/utils/guild_tabs/audit_log/AuditLogChannelMessages.ts:45
msgid "{actor} created the category {channel}"
msgstr "{actor} đã tạo danh mục {channel}"

